      "subject": "elective",
      "material": "terms",
      "term": "Transfer Learning Workflow",
      "definition": "1.Load a pretrained model. Choose a CNN trained on a large dataset (ResNet, MobileNet, or EfficientNet). Remove its original classification layer.\n2.Add a new classification layer matching your number of classes.\n3.Freeze the pretrained layers. Their weights stay fixed. This preserves the general visual features (edges, textures, shapes) and reduces computation.\n4.Train the new classification head on your dataset. It learns to map the frozen features to your new labels.\n5.Fine-tune (optional). After the new head has converged, unfreeze some or all pretrained layers and continue training with a very low learning rate.",
      "pdfWording": "1.Load a pretrained model. Choose a CNN trained on a large dataset (ResNet, MobileNet, or EfficientNet). Remove its original classification layer.\n2.Add a new classification layer matching your number of classes.\n3.Freeze the pretrained layers. Their weights stay fixed. This preserves the general visual features (edges, textures, shapes) and reduces computation.\n4.Train the new classification head on your dataset. It learns to map the frozen features to your new labels.\n5.Fine-tune (optional). After the new head has converged, unfreeze some or all pretrained layers and continue training with a very low learning rate.",
      "contentKind": "slide-excerpt",
      "questionStyle": "heading",
      "questionExcerpt": "1.Load a pretrained model. Choose a CNN trained on a large dataset (ResNet, MobileNet, or EfficientNet). Remove its original classification layer.\n2.Add a new classification layer matching your number of classes.\n3.Freeze the pretrained layers. Their weights stay fixed. This preserves the general visual features (edges, textures, shapes) and reduces computation.\n4.Train the new classification head on your dataset. It learns to map the frozen features to your new labels.\n5.Fine-tune (optional). After the new head has converged, unfreeze some or all pretrained layers and continue training with a very low learning rate.",
