      "definition": "The process of identifying and keeping only the most relevant input variables to improve model performance. Irrelevant or redundant features introduce noise, increase computational overhead, and risk overfitting—a problem known as the curse of dimensionality—which reduces a model's ability to generalize to new data.\nBy removing useless variables using statistical tests, correlation analysis, or algorithm feature importance, you streamline training time, reduce complexity, and boost prediction accuracy.",
